Hi, my teacher assigned a piece of homework involving universe, and I never learned it before. Please help!



Question: Let $A =$ {a, b, d, f, g} and $B$ be a sets in the universe $U$ $=$ {letters of the alphabet.} If $A \cap B = $ {b, d}, which could be set $B$?



Choices:

a. $B = $ {b, d, g}

b. $B = $ {b, d, k}

c. $B = $ {b, d, 5, e}

d. $B = $ {a, f, g}



I'm not asking for an answer, but if anyone can explain to me what is universe and how I'm suppose to solve this problem, that will be helpful. Thank you so much!!!
